hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:
"263","On the blood-money of a dhimmi: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya Abu Muhammad narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The blood-money of every covenanted person, while in his covenant, is one thousand dinars."
"264","Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Faris narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, who said: [The Messenger of Allah] (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For the male organ, the blood-money."
"265","[And with the same chain:] That [the Prophet] (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decreed for the two hands the blood-money, and for the two feet the blood-money."
"266","[And with the same chain:] From al-Zuhri, that al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The woman - her paternal relatives pay her blood-money, and her sons inherit from her. Abu Dawud said: Yahya ibn Yaman narrated it from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from al-Mughirah, and it is a mistake."
"267","Muhammad ibn al-Wazir al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Yahya, meaning Ibn Hassan, narrated to us, Mujammi' ibn Ya'qub narrated to us. Rabi'ah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman informed me, who said: The blood-money of a dhimmi was like that of a Muslim in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the time of Abu Bakr, the time of Umar, and the time of Uthman, until it was the beginning - meaning of the rule of Mu'awiyah - when Mu'awiyah said: If his family have been afflicted by his loss, the treasury of the Muslims has been afflicted by his loss as well; so make for the treasury of the Muslims half, and for his family half: five hundred dinars and five hundred dinars. Then another man of the dhimmah was killed, and Mu'awiyah said: If we were to look at what enters the treasury and make it a stipend for the Muslims and their defense - he said: from then on he fixed his blood-money at five hundred."
